# SCENARIO: fix_119_bot_walk_cam   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: auto   BOTCFG: off
# Fix #119, bot's-eye check: a REAL bot walk temple -> ammo shop z6, commanded in-band and watched
# through that bot's own operator camera (the camera's LocalPlayer IS the bot, so its self_pos stream
# is the bot's own walk as its client renders it). fix_119_route_no_backtrack only prices the route
# with `/cavebot route`; this proves the live walker takes it.
# Run: runner.py fix_119_bot_walk_cam.steps --var BOT=<Thais bot>   (used: Kaelis Duke)
# The scenario pins $BOT (`reload debug,$BOT`): debug isolation despawns every other bot until a
# restart, so restart canary afterwards (systemctl stop/start) to bring the population back.
# Route (`/cavebot route`, b4_b5): leg 1 temple (32369,32237,7) -> stairs UP (32350,32246,7) = 66
# tiles, final leg landing (32350,32245,6) -> (32345,32246,6) = 6 tiles, 72 in all, 0 revisits.
# Acceptance, from BOTH layers:
#   server (audit, named watch): a path search from the z6 landing to the goal succeeds, a probe
#     stands ON the goal tile, no pathout stuck/abandoned/osc, no failed walk search to the goal;
#   camera (the bot's own view): `self` ends at (32345,32246,6); the walk went z7 -> z6 (the stairs
#     up), revisited no tile and reversed no step (walk-check), in 60..80 steps (route: 72).
# Walk-pauses (#120) are observer-gated and the camera IS an observer, so the walk may stop for up to
# 20 s a few times: the 100 s wait covers that; pauses do not create revisits (walkpause is audited).
# First run (f119_cam1, 2026-11-19, 5f19be19c): reached the goal over the planned stairs, server
# clean (one 66-tile astar-direct search, arrived, no stuck), but walk-check FAILED: 89 steps,
# 4 revisits. Not a planning fault: a Rat stood on the next queued tile (32356,32238,7) at step 30; the failed
# step pops its direction anyway (Creature::onCreatureWalk), the rest of the queue ran one tile off,
# ~11 more directions were burned against walls in 2.5 s (probe pathLen 22->9 with 2 moves), and the
# path's last 8 moves (N,E,N,E x5) executed from (32354,32248,7), walking the bot 6 tiles east
# before the queue drained and the engine re-planned. The second real walk
# (f119_blk2) walked 71 steps, 0 revisits. The check stays strict: it is what catches that bug.
@srv cmd _global "reload debug,$BOT"
@srv sleep 20
@srv audit kinds probe,path,pathout,state,walkpause,cmd
@srv audit watch "$BOT"
@srv audit on expect="enabled=on"
@srv cmd "$BOT" teleport 32369,32237,7 expect="teleported to \(32369,32237,7\)"
@srv sleep 3
@cam:$BOT login
@cam:$BOT perceive expect="tap=true"
@cam:$BOT self expect="pos=32369,32237,7"
@srv audit mark "F119CAM goto ammo 32345,32246,6 from the temple"
@srv cmd "$BOT" goto 32345,32246,6 via=cam expect="walking to \(32345,32246,6\)"
@srv sleep 100
@cam:$BOT self expect="pos=32345,32246,6"
@cam:$BOT walk-check end=32345,32246,6 z-seq=7,6 max-revisits=0 max-osc=0 min-steps=60 max-steps=80
@cam:$BOT dump-view
@cam:$BOT view
@srv audit mark "F119CAM end"
# (the path record's own `src` field collides with the `src=` stream filter: match the bot's pos)
@srv expect src=srv:audit k=path bot=$BOT pos~="x.: 32350, .y.: 32245, .z.: 6\}" dst~="^.32345, 32246, 6.$" result=ok min=1 within=130
@srv expect src=srv:audit k=probe bot=$BOT pos~="x.: 32345, .y.: 32246, .z.: 6\}" min=1 within=130
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=pathout bot=$BOT outcome~="^(stuck|abandoned|osc)$" within=130
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=path bot=$BOT dst~="^.32345, 32246, 6.$" planner~="^(astar|jitter|wide|astar-chunk|astar-offset)$" result~="^fail" within=130
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=150
@cam:$BOT logout
@srv audit watch clear
@srv audit off
